==Strategy==
This stage is very cash generous at the beginning, so be sure to stall to max out your wallet with the Mooths and B.B.Bunnies before hitting the base. 

===Recommended units===
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Best to use when Red EnerG pushes.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: His anti-Behemoth and Red abilities are great against the Ragin' Gories and Bunnies. He can only land occasional hits on Red EnerGs with lucky timings though.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: Pushes back and Freezes Relic enemies so you can get to the pesky Red EnerG(s), and also deal chip damage to any enemies.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: He's Immune to Surges from the Red EnerG(s), is Strong against and will greatly slow the Relics. His Surges also do good damage to anything.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kuu γ]]: Her being Strong against Reds/Darks lets her deal heavy damage to most of the enemies here. If you have her Relic targeting unlocked, she can be one of the best units for this stage.
*[[Metal Maiden Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Sonic Siren Koneko]]: Koneko does very well here thanks to her suite of abilities that cripple the EnerGs and Jackrabbits. Just be mindful that Bun Bun is counterintuitively not Floating, and plan the rest of your lineup accordingly.

